# check_pack_refs.py allowlist -- references that are INTENTIONALLY not files of this pack.
# One fnmatch pattern per line: `<ref-pattern>` or `<citing-file-pattern>::<ref-pattern>`.
# Never add a real broken pointer here: fix the pointer.

# Run artifacts: files a run writes into $WORK, named so the reader knows what to look for.
decision_log.md
skeptic_review.md
closure_review.md
round_ledger.md
job_description.md
summary.md
report.md
COMMANDMENT.md
notes.md
# Host / agent memory files (Claude Code), not pack files.
CLAUDE.md
MEMORY.md
# Upstream sibling packs: the tile-programming-triton front end (not vendored in GEAK) and its
# scripts / pages, plus the NVIDIA packs a cross-reference names. Each citing line says so.
scripts/plain_autotune.py
scripts/knob_expose.py
scripts/knob_probe.py
scripts/champion_emit.py
scripts/ttgir_facts.py
search-routing.md
triton-negative-patterns.md
nvidia-sm12x.md
*references/method/profile.md::references/companion-tools.md
*references/method/profile.md::references/dsl/cutedsl/references/companion-tools.md
# Placeholders in prose explaining the citation syntax itself.
*references/method/orchestration.md::file.md*
# JSON-schema self reference: resolved relative to the stage cards in runtime/stages/, not the schema.
*runtime/stage-card.schema.json::../stage-card.schema.json
# check_term_index.py's own selftest fixtures (strings that build a throwaway pack).
*scripts/check_term_index.py::*
